# Copy to .dev.vars (gitignored). Values here are Worker bindings for `wrangler dev` only.
# They do NOT change which Cloudflare account wrangler deploys to.
# Deploy ONLY with ~/RamenProtocol/_ops/infra/ramen-deploy.sh — it refuses unless the Ramen
# account id and token are set, so the global wrangler login is never used.

# Plan 4 (optional). Webhooks are refused until PAYPAL_WEBHOOK_ID is set.
# PAYPAL_WEBHOOK_ID=
# Sandbox PERSONAL accounts that receive demo payouts (unset -> example.com addresses that stay UNCLAIMED).
# PAYPAL_RECEIVER_ROOM=
# PAYPAL_RECEIVER_OPENER=
# PAYPAL_RECEIVER_ARTIST=

# Judge pass (Dec 1-15). NEVER put a real value in this file or commit one. In production set these with `wrangler secret put`.
# The code judges type into the "For judges" box (8 to 64 characters, letters, digits, - and _). Give it to judges only through
# Devpost's private testing-instructions field. It unlocks the reserved demo copies and AI calls. Unset: nobody is a judge.
# JUDGE_CODE=
# A second sandbox BUYER login shown only after a valid judge code, so a changed public password can't lock judges out.
# Both must be set. Unset: judges keep seeing the public login.
# JUDGE_BUYER_EMAIL=
# JUDGE_BUYER_PASSWORD=
